waydroid-host-stack: DuplicateData on the discovery filters.

Without it BlueZ (src/device.c device_set_rssi, RSSI_THRESHOLD 8)
reports a known device again only when its RSSI moved by 8 dBm or its
advertising data changed, and the bridge turns only those property
changes into AdvReports for the guest.  A steady advertiser seen once,
a parked car at -36 dBm, was reported by the controller at every scan
cycle (btmon, 22 reports in 20 min) but reached Android 4 times, none
inside the Tesla app's 10 s scans, which ended with "no_peripherals"
(Pro1x, 2026-11-23).  With DuplicateData BlueZ treats the discovery as
filtered and emits RSSI on every report the controller passes (about
one per device every 7-10 s on the Pro1x's WCN3990, measured with
bluetoothctl and dbus-monitor, 2026-11-27).  Ours (fxtec-pro1x-guix,
2026-11-27), on d9a316e (MIT), after
waydroid-host-stack-gatt-write-parts.patch.

--- a/host/src/bluez/mod.rs	2026-11-27 02:34:10.395857128 +0100
+++ b/host/src/bluez/mod.rs	2026-11-27 02:33:17.554295624 +0100
@@ -221,14 +221,21 @@
         // Dual (auto): BR/EDR inquiry + LE so guest Settings Inquiry can see
         // classic devices (e.g. Xbox) while LE (Hue) still works.
         let transport_name = guest_pair_discovery_transport();
+        // DuplicateData: without it BlueZ reports a device again only when
+        // its RSSI moved by 8 dBm or its data changed, so a steady
+        // advertiser seen once (a parked car) never reaches a guest scan
+        // started later.  With it, every report the controller passes
+        // becomes a property change (RSSI, data) and so an AdvReport.
         let filter = bluer::DiscoveryFilter {
             transport: bluer_transport(transport_name),
+            duplicate_data: true,
             ..Default::default()
         };
         info!(
             transport = transport_name.as_bluez_str(),
             classic = transport_name.includes_classic(),
             le = transport_name.includes_le(),
+            duplicate_data = true,
             "setting discovery filter for guest pair scan"
         );
         adapter
